/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  curate25_vp_dimethylethanolamine -- the vapour pressure of dimethylethanolamine, REFITTED to
  measurements (DEV.md 4c C281 steps 2 and 3).  Written by `bin/choupo-curate
  vp dimethylethanolamine`; everything above the RESULT paragraph is the DECLARATION,
  committed before any fit ran, so it can be read against the result.

  WHY.  The catalogue record carried `vaporPressure { model AmbroseWalton; }`,
  a corresponding-states ESTIMATE from Tc, Pc and omega that never reads the
  record's own Tb (C279 measured a median 19.6 % AAD over the 25 such records
  with archive data).  Here a three-parameter Antoine is fitted to ONE
  laboratory and held out on ANOTHER that shares no author with it.

  STUDIES (one per article, extracted by `choupo-thermoml extract-vp`; ranked
  by points, ties by DOI):
      10.1021/je049761y                29 pts  277.9-316.3 K  Kapteina; Slovik; Verevkin; Heintz
      10.1016/j.jct.2013.03.020        25 pts  273.15-363.15 K  Chiali-Baba-Ahmed; Dergal; Negadi; Mokbel
      10.1021/je101259r                15 pts  309.5-447.8 K  Klepacova; Huttenhuis; Derks; Versteeg
  SET ASIDE BY NAME:
      (none)

  PARTITION (the C16 rule, declared): FIT = the study with the most points,
  doi 10.1021/je049761y (29 pts, 277.9-316.3 K); HELD OUT =
  the next largest sharing no author with it, doi 10.1016/j.jct.2013.03.020 (25 pts,
  273.15-363.15 K).

  BAND: maxAAD 2.2 % (declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 25 points (2.01 to 2.82 %, mean 2.165 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean).

  NORMAL BOILING POINT: the record's Tb 404.15 K lies OUTSIDE the measured span 273.15-363.15 K: the fitted Antoine's own normal boiling point (P = 101.325 kPa) must lie within 2 K of it, or the fit is NOT promoted (an extrapolation that misses the record's own boiling point).

  OBJECTIVE (C281 step 3, declared): `objective { method twoStage; }` --
  Vitor's fitting practice (DEV.md 4c C280): least squares in log10 P for a
  first estimate, then the LARGEST relative error in P, (P_model - P)/P, over
  the fit points minimised from it; both answers are kept in the result.  A
  student who prefers another objective declares `leastSquares` or `minimax`.

  EARLIER FIT, SUPERSEDED BY THIS DECLARATION
  @@EARLIER-BEGIN@@
  C281 step 2, objective leastSquares (log10 P), the same partition and
  band: WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 14.191855 - 9599.5633/(T + 289.4230),
  in-sample R2 0.998529 over 29 points, 277.9-316.3 K. HELD OUT: 25
  points, AAD 12.9406 % against the band 2.2 % -> notValidated. Its own
  normal boiling point (101.325 kPa): 387.26 K. NOT PROMOTED: held-out
  verdict notValidated (AAD 12.94 % against the band 2.2 % declared
  before the fit); the record keeps AmbroseWalton
  @@EARLIER-END@@

  NO MEASURED POINT IS IN THIS TREE: constant/archiveDatasets declares both
  series by DOI, NIST URL and sha256; `bin/choupo-curate fetch` regenerates
  them into constant/archiveExtracts/ (gitignored).

  RESULT
  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Objective twoStage. Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 7.287831 - 3246.8966/(T +
  46.1092), in-sample R2 0.998315 over 29 points, 277.9-316.3 K. HELD
  OUT: 25 points, AAD 8.3129 % (max 11.9823 %) against the band 2.2 % ->
  notValidated; the stage-1 least-squares answer on the same points: AAD
  12.9406 %, max 40.0319 %. Its own normal boiling point (101.325 kPa):
  399.76 K. NOT PROMOTED: held-out verdict notValidated (AAD 8.313 %
  against the band 2.2 % declared before the fit); the record keeps
  AmbroseWalton
  @@RESULT-END@@
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name       fit_antoine;
        type       vaporPressureFit;
        component  dimethylethanolamine;

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/dimethylethanolamine-vapourPressure-je049761y.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je049761y"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/dimethylethanolamine-vapourPressure-j.jct.2013.03.020.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1016/j.jct.2013.03.020"; }
                role      validation;
            }
        );

        acceptance
        {
            maxAAD  2.2 percent;
            origin  "declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 25 points (2.01 to 2.82 %, mean 2.165 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean";
        }

        objective  { method twoStage; }

        output     { file fit_antoine.csv; }
    }
);
